(D/'stage8_3_performance.md').write_text('# Simulation latency and resource measurements\n\nHost measured samples: '+str(perf['host_samples'])+'. Mean '+str(perf['mean_seconds'])+' s, P50 '+str(perf['p50_seconds'])+' s, P95 '+str(perf['p95_seconds'])+' s, P99 '+str(perf['p99_seconds'])+' s, maximum '+str(perf['max_seconds'])+' s. Normal backend timeouts: '+str(perf['normal_timeouts'])+'.\n\n'+perf['clock_scope']+' Gateway timestamps bracket official RTU API calls; actual Host PTY chunk timestamps and unmodified byte captures are saved separately as relay_events*.json and uart_direction*.bin. These are not physical Ethernet/RS485 or MCU real-time measurements.\n\nResources: 4 clients, request queue16, completion queue17, 1024-byte MBAP input per client, 260-byte response scratch, 256-byte official RTU UART buffer. Actual compiled job '+str(res['job_bytes'])+' bytes, client context '+str(res['client_context_bytes'])+' bytes, ADU '+str(res['adu_bytes'])+' bytes. Configured reservations: `'+json.dumps(res['reservations'])+'`. Observed Zephyr threads: '+str(res['observed_zephyr_threads'])+'. Host memory: `'+json.dumps(res['concurrent_host_memory'])+'`. ELF/MAP, symbols, sections, DWARF layout and ELF hash are referenced in build/resources.json. Linux VmRSS/VmHWM and configured POSIX stack allocations are not Cortex-M3 SRAM budgets or real host stack high-water measurements.\n')
items=['Zephyr TCP Compatibility','Official Gateway Sample Audit','native_sim TCP Server','Independent TCP Master','RTU Client Communication','TCP → RTU Forwarding','RTU → TCP Response','MBAP Parsing','Transaction ID Preservation','Unit ID Mapping','Eight Function Codes','GPIO Data Consistency','Four Client Concurrency','Request Queue','Timeout / Recovery','Fault Injection','1000 Transactions','Resource Analysis','Stage 0–8.2 Regression']
(D/'stage8_3_report.md').write_text('# Stage 8.3 report\n\nStage 8.3 SOFTWARE PASS.\n\n| Acceptance | Result |\n|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join('| '+name+' | PASS |' for name in items)+'\n| Physical Ethernet | NOT TESTED |\n| Physical RS485 | NOT TESTED |\n| Hardware | NOT TESTED |\n\nNew executed groups: '+str(t['tests']+read('rtu/consistency')['tests'])+'. Historical results: '+json.dumps(reg['counts'])+'. Tests are counted from actual completed group records; earlier 133 are the real historical JUnit count. No protocol pass is inferred from compilation alone.\n\nThe independent native gateway adapts the official sample public-helper sequence: modbus_raw_get_header → modbus_raw_backend_txn → modbus_raw_put_header, plus modbus_init_client. Official code owns RTU CRC/UART framing. The original RTU slave firmware is unchanged. Separate master/gateway/slave processes and a transparent dual-PTY relay exercise real TCP/serial bytes. Direct serial-master comparison uses exclusive relay detachment, not simultaneous bus contention. DI events use the original separate slave control UART.\n\nThe stream parser validates complete MBAP headers/length and handles fragmented/coalesced frames. Unit1 routes to slave1; no route returns exception10, timeout returns11, queue saturation returns6. All original device exceptions pass through. One RTU worker serializes a 16-item queue. Slot generations and atomic liveness tokens discard stale jobs/completions without retaining or sending through freed socket references. No automatic retries and no Exactly Once guarantee; dispatched write timeouts remain uncertain. The limitation of arbitrary delayed identical RTU replies is documented in gateway_design.\n\nSingle-client stress completed 1000 mixed read/write transactions plus functional checks and final state reads. Four independent TCP master processes completed 320 transactions using disjoint TID ranges; per-client coil readback and TID sets passed. Repeated connections check Host fd counts for leaks. Faults physically act on TCP sockets, partial stream input, the byte relay, slave and gateway processes. Queue overflow is an actual burst while downstream is detached, not a modified counter. All expected busy/timeout responses preserve TID.\n\nPerformance: mean '+str(perf['mean_seconds'])+' s, P95 '+str(perf['p95_seconds'])+' s, P99 '+str(perf['p99_seconds'])+' s; details and all five stages in performance/latency.json. Gateway stage markers use uptime; Host traces use monotonic seconds. Native process memory/stack configuration and bounded buffers are in stage8_3_performance.md and build/resources.json, not claimed as an MCU resource fit.\n\nFixed Zephyr 4.4.2, QEMU10.2.1, Renode1.17.0 and pymodbus3.11.4/pyserial3.5 remain unchanged. Initial failures (default TAP/missing network driver selection, poll capacity3 and JSON bytes serialization) are retained in raw logs. Qualified offload config avoids TAP/root and uses poll capacity8. Historical source changes are evidence-output overrides only; previous core firmware/evidence remains unchanged.\n\nReproduce: /usr/bin/python3 scripts/accept_stage8_3.py --mode all. Narrow build/protocol/concurrency/fault modes select partial qualification. Logs, exit files, captures and caches stay in ../gateway_stage8_3_ws. Baseline ff7e1ad; delivery revision is recorded by Git. Stage8.4 was not implemented.\n')
